<p>In this demo, we automatically deduce a FlashAttention kernel with ~25 lines of SQL, which just expresses vanilla attention. This is possible due to three portable SQL extensions that we’re building:
- xarray-sql: a library that efficiently represents petabyte scale array datasets in the cloud as tables (relations).
- ddx: a database extension that adds automatic differentiation in the style of JAX to standard SQL, assuming the above array data model.
- einfold: a modular query planner for fast tensor contractions in vanilla SQL, again, assuming the above array data model.<p>My hope is that the relational model and algebra provide fresh perspectives on how we might do accelerator programming. Here, our thesis is that separating the logical layers in a tensor program from the physical layers is both more correct and more scalable.<p>If the Bitter Lesson is a central dogma of machine learning, then why not formalize it with relational algebra?<p>If this interests you and you’d like to tinker with us at the intersection of database theory and ML systems, join us on Discord at <a href="https://xql.systems" rel="nofollow">https://xql.systems</a>  (link at the bottom). Cheers.</p>
<hr>
